    "linear": "As fullscale, with a bitmap walk in place of Cartesian merge sorting. This diagnostic built an explicit vector of consecutive IDs; the final implementation iterates them directly.",
    "selected-seven": "Same fullscale executable; changed only the first periodic threshold to 2,000,000.",
    "order-base": "Unmodified Core following original enabledness support; exact source of #1350 on main.",
    "order-new": "Only bitmap enumeration and direct iteration of canonical IDs. Sparse indices and low dense occupancy fall back to the previous cancellable sort.",
    "production-storage": "Windowed original enabledness on main, packed-product prototypes excluded. Explicit component/prefix fractions 1/16 and 1/64, capped at 512 and 128 MiB respectively. Dense discovery supplies Cartesian order directly. One worker, default prefix schedule, 240 s. This binary includes the main successor assignment improvement (#1357), without the producer-action images (#1358).",
    "integrated": "Same dense storage policy at 8 GiB and direct Cartesian iteration with #1358, on the earlier developer base. Four periodic checks. No edge packing. A separate 240 s run."
  },
